n- Click \\\\\"Create merge request\\\\\" in the notification banner\\\\n- Update MR title to match requirements (e.g., \\\\\"Update contribution document\\\\\")\\\\n- Create the merge request\\\\n\\\\n### 6. Verify Merge Request\\\\n- Confirm MR ID appears in URL (e.g., /merge_requests/217)\\\\n- Verify title, source, and target branches are correct\\\\n- Check that changes are properly displayed\\\\n\\\\n## Notes\\\\n- The contribution document should be comprehensive and cover multiple development approaches\\\\n- Include practical examples and code snippets where appropriate\\\\n- Ensure all three required subtitles are included\\\\n- The merge request title should match the specific task requirement\\\\n\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'UpdateContributionDocument'}), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"\\ngoto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/')\\nnoop(2000)  # Wait for page to load\\n\", thought='Perfect! I have a detailed SOP to follow. Let me start by accessing the GitLab instance and cloning the repository.', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action=<ActionType.BROWSE_INTERACTIVE: 'browse_interactive'>, security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  *     * [ New project/repository  ](/projects/new)\\n    * [ New group  ](/groups/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/-/snippets/new)\\n\\n\\n\\nAdministrator user\u2019s menu \\n\\n  *     * [ Administrator  @root  ](/root)\\n  *     * Set status \\n    * [ Edit profile  ](/-/user_settings/profile)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/-/profile/preferences)\\n  *     * [ Sign out  ](/users/sign_out)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ 84  ](/dashboard/issues?assignee_username=root)\\n\\n99+ \\n\\n  * Merge requests \\n\\n    * [ Assigned  7  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?assignee_username=root)\\n    * [ R