com](mailto:prokilchu@gmail.com \"prokilchu@gmail.com\")>\\n\\nUnverified \\n\\n8568cfb8 \\n\\n  * Contributing \\n  * How Can I Contribute? \\n  * Understanding Sotopia\\'s CodeBase \\n  * Sending Pull Requests to Sotopia \\n  * 1\\\\. Fork the Official Repository \\n  * 2\\\\. Configure Git \\n  * 3\\\\. Synchronize with Official Repository \\n  * 4\\\\. Set up the Development Environment \\n  * 5\\\\. Write Code and Commit It \\n  * 6\\\\. Open a Pull Request \\n  * PR Rules \\n  * 1\\\\. Pull Request title \\n  * 2\\\\. Pull Request description \\n\\n\\n\\n**contribution.md** 4.29 KiB \\n\\nBlame \\n\\nEdit \\n\\n  *     * Open in Web IDE  ` . ` Quickly and easily edit multiple files in your project. \\n\\n    * [ Edit single file  Edit this file only.  ](/root/sotopia/-/edit/main/docs/pages/contribution/contribution.md?ref_type=heads)\\n\\n\\n\\nReplace  Delete \\n\\n[ ](/root/sotopia/-/raw/main/docs/pages/contribution/contribution.md?ref_type=heads \"Open raw\") [ ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia/-/raw/main/docs/pages/contribution/contribution.md?ref_type=heads&inline=false \"Download\")\\n\\n#  <::after> Contributing \\n\\nThanks for your interest in contributing to Sotopia! We welcome and appreciate contributions. \\n\\n##  <::after> How Can I Contribute? \\n\\nThere are many ways that you can contribute: \\n\\n  1. <::marker> **Download and use** Sotopia, and send [ issues ](https://github.com/sotopia-lab/sotopia/issues) when you encounter something that isn\\'t working or a feature that you\\'d like to see. \\n  2. <::marker> **Send feedback** after each session by using our feedback mechanisms (if implemented), so we can see where things are working and failing, and also build an open dataset for training social agents. \\n  3. <::marker> **Improve the Codebase** by sending PRs (see details below). In particular, we have some [ good first issue ](https://github.com/sotopia-lab/sotopia/labels/good%20first%20issue) issues that may be ones to start on. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Understanding Sotopia\\'s CodeBase \\n\\nTo understand the codebase, please refer to the README in each module: \\n\\n  * <::marker> [ sotopia ](/root/sotopia/-/blob/main/./sotopia/README.md)\\n  * <::marker> [ docs ](/root/sotopia/-/blob/main/./docs/README.md)\\n  * <::marker> [ tests ](/root/sotopia/-/blob/main/./tests/README.md)\\n\\n\\n\\nWhen you write code, it is also good to write tests. Please navigate to the ` tests ` folder to see existing test suites. At the moment, we have different kinds of tests including unit tests and integration tests. Please refer to the README for each test suite. These tests also run on GitHub\\'s continuous integration to ensure quality of the project. \\n\\n##  <::after> Sending Pull Requests to Sotopia \\n\\n###  <::after> 1\\\\. Fork the Official Repository \\n\\nFork the [ Sotopia repository ](https://github.com/sotopia-lab/sotopia) into your own account. Clone your own forked repository into your local environment: \\n    \\n    \\n    git clone git@github.com:/sotopia.git\\n\\n###  <::after> 2\\\\. Configure Git \\n\\nSet the official repository as your [ upstream ](https://www.atlassian.com/git/tutorials/git-forks-and-upstreams) to synchronize with the latest update in the official repository. Add the original repository as upstream: \\n    \\n    \\n    cd sotopia\\n    git remote add upstream git@github.com:sotopia-lab/sotopia.git\\n\\nVerify that the remote is set: \\n    \\n    \\n    git remote -v\\n\\nYou should see both ` origin ` and ` upstream ` in the output. \\n\\n###  <::after> 3\\\\. Synchronize with Official Repository \\n\\nSynchronize latest commit with official repository before coding: \\n    \\n    \\n    git fetch upstream\\n    git checkout main\\n    git merge upstream/main\\n    git push origin main\\n\\n###  <::after> 4\\\\. Set up the Development Environment \\n\\n?? @ProKil \\n\\n###  <::after> 5\\\\. Write Code and Commit It \\n\\nOnce you have done this, you can write code, test it, and commit it to a branch (replace ` my_branch ` with an appropriate name): \\n    \\n    \\n    git checkout -b my_branch\\n    git add .\\n    git commit\\n    git push origin my_branch\\n\\n###  <::after> 6\\\\. Open a Pull Request \\n\\n  * <::marker>On GitHub, go to the page of your forked repository, and create a Pull Request: \\n    * <::marker>Click on ` Branches `\\n    * <::marker>Click on the ` ... ` beside your branch and click on ` New pull request `\\n    * <::marker>Set ` base repository ` to ` sotopia-lab/sotopia `\\n    * <::marker>Set ` base ` to ` main `\\n    * <::marker>Click ` Create pull request `\\n\\n\\n\\nThe PR should appear in [ Sotopia PRs ](https://github.com/sotopia-lab/sotopia/pulls) . \\n\\nThen the Sotopia team will review your code. \\n\\n##  <::after> PR Rules \\n\\n###  <::after> 1\\\\. Pull Request title \\n\\nAs described [ here ](https://github.com/commitizen/conventional-commit-types/blob/master/index.json) , a valid PR title should begin with one of the following prefixes: \\n\\n  * <::marker> ` feat ` : A new feature \\n  * <::marker> ` fix ` : A bug fix \\n  * <::marker> ` docs ` : Documentation only changes \\n  * <::marker> ` style ` : Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code (white space, formatting, missing semicolons, etc.) \\n  * <::marker> ` refactor ` : A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature \\n  * <::marker> ` perf ` : A code change that improves performance \\n  * <::marker> ` test ` : Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests \\n  * <::marker> ` build ` : Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies (example scopes: gulp, broccoli, npm) \\n  * <::marker> ` ci ` : Changes to our CI configuration files and scripts (example scopes: Travis, Circle, BrowserStack, SauceLabs) \\n  * <::marker> ` chore ` : Other changes that don\\'t modify src or test files \\n  * <::marker> ` revert ` : Reverts a previous commit \\n\\n\\n\\nFor example, a PR title could be: \\n\\n  * <::marker> ` refactor: modify package path `\\n  * <::marker> ` feat(frontend): xxxx ` , where ` (frontend) ` means that this PR mainly focuses on the frontend component. \\n\\n\\n\\nYou may also check out previous PRs in the [ PR list ](https://github.com/sotopia-lab/sotopia/pulls) . \\n\\n###  <::after> 2\\\\. Pull Request description \\n\\n  * <::marker>If your PR is small (such as a typo fix), you can go brief. \\n  * <::marker>If it contains a lot of changes, it\\'s better to write more details. \\n\\n\\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia/-/blob/main/docs/pages/contribution/contribution.md?ref_type=heads', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', screenshot_path='/outputs/.browser_screenshots/screenshot_20251101_105954_253484.png', error=False, observation=<ObservationType.BROWSE: 'browse'>, goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia/-/blob/main/docs/pages/contribution/contribution.md?ref_type=heads'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"\\n\\n\\n\\nclick('2245')  # Click on the contribution.md file\\nnoop(2000)  # Wait for page to load\\n\\n\\n\\n\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='85'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"\\n\\n\\n\\nclick('2394')  # Click on the Edit button\\nnoop(2000)  # Wait for page to load\\n\\n\\n\\n\", thought='Perfect! I can see the current contribution.md file. Now I need to edit it to add the three required sections about development environments. Let me click the Edit button to modify the file.', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action=<ActionType.BROWSE_INTERACTIVE: 'browse_interactive'>, security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  * In this project \\n\\n    * [ New issue  ](/root/sotopia/-/issues/new)\\n    * [ New merge request  ](/root/sotopia/-/merge_requests/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/root/sot